%description:
Tests dropSynData, the SYN data of Linux. The client sends 1400 bytes on a
Fast Open SYN, and the tester removes the Fast Open option, so the server gets
a SYN with data and without Fast Open. With dropSynData, the server drops the
data, as Linux tcp_conn_request() does, and the SYN-ACK acknowledges only the
SYN; the client sends the 1400 bytes again, and the server acknowledges them
segment by segment (B003, B004). Without it, the server keeps the data in its
receive queue (RFC 9293 section 3.10.7.2) and acknowledges all 1400 bytes at
the first segment.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.fastOpen=true
*.cli_app.tOpen2=0.5s
*.cli_app.active2=true
*.cli_app.localPort2=1001
*.cli_app.tSend2=0.5s
*.cli_app.sendBytes2=1400B
*.cli_app.fastOpen2=true
*.srv_app.tOpen2=0.5s
*.srv_app.localPort2=2000

*.tcptester.script="a3 strip 34"
*.srv_tcp.dropSynData = true
*.srv_tcp.mss = 1460
*.cli_tcp.mss = 536
*.cli_tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.srv_tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.501 A003] A.1001 > B.2000: S 125000:126400(1400) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize NOP NOP# removing options
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[0.503 B002] A.1001 < B.2000: A S 125500:125500(0) ack 125001 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[0.505 A004] A.1001 > B.2000: A 125001:125537(536) ack 125501 win 16384 
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[0.707 B003] A.1001 < B.2000: A ack 125537 win 16384 
[0.709 A005] A.1001 > B.2000: A 125537:126073(536) ack 125501 win 16384 
[0.709 A006] A.1001 > B.2000: A 126073:126401(328) ack 125501 win 16384 
[0.911 B004] A.1001 < B.2000: A ack 126401 win 16384 
[0.912] tcpdump finished, A:6 B:4 segments
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
